Teach jq's two bundled `config.sub` copies about Apple's iOS-simulator host
triplet.

`build.sh` configures jq with `--host=$HOST_TRIPLET`, and forge builds three
iOS slices: `arm64-apple-ios` (device), `arm64-apple-ios-simulator` and
`x86_64-apple-ios-simulator`. autoconf canonicalises the `--host` value through
the bundled `config.sub` before anything is compiled. For the simulator name
that script yields machine `<cpu>-apple` and OS `ios-simulator`, then splits
the OS on its dash into kernel `ios` and OS `simulator`. The bare word
`simulator` gets past the recognised-OS list only by accident -- it matches the
unrelated `sim*` entry meant for bare-metal simulator targets -- and then
reaches the block that validates kernel/OS *pairs*, which knows nothing about
`ios` + `simulator` and falls through to its catch-all:

    Invalid configuration `arm64-apple-ios-simulator': Kernel `ios' not known
    to work with OS `simulator'.

configure exits there, before any compilation. `arm64-apple-ios` and every
Android triplet canonicalise fine; only the two simulator slices die.

Both hunks make the same one-line addition -- an empty `ios-simulator)` case in
the kernel/OS pairing block, next to the existing `*-eabi*` entry -- but they
have to be applied to two different files, because jq's build validates the
same `--host` value twice:

  1. `config/config.sub` (jq 1.7.1 ships the 2022-01-03 vintage) is what jq's
     own top-level configure uses.

  2. `modules/oniguruma/config.sub` (an older 2020-08-17 vintage, hence the
     different line number for the same block) belongs to the vendored
     oniguruma copy. `build.sh` passes `--with-oniguruma=builtin`, which makes
     jq's configure.ac take the `AC_CONFIG_SUBDIRS([modules/oniguruma])` path,
     so oniguruma's own configure re-runs with the same `--host` and
     re-validates it with *its* config.sub. Patching only jq's copy just moves
     the same error one directory down.

Without both hunks, two of the three iOS slices of flet-libjq fail at
configure, and the `jq` recipe -- which static-links libjq.a and libonig.a out
of this recipe -- has no iOS wheels. Android is unaffected either way.

The commit that introduced this file (ec8d184, a bulk branch consolidation)
records no rationale; the account above is reconstructed from the diff,
jq's configure.ac, and running both config.sub copies against forge's triplets,
patched and unpatched.

diff --git a/config/config.sub b/config/config.sub
index dba16e8..215b8e2 100755
--- a/config/config.sub
+++ b/config/config.sub
@@ -1792,6 +1792,8 @@ case $kernel-$os in
 		;;
 	*-eabi* | *-gnueabi*)
 		;;
+	ios-simulator)
+		;;
 	-*)
 		# Blank kernel with real OS is always fine.
 		;;
diff --git a/modules/oniguruma/config.sub b/modules/oniguruma/config.sub
index 0753e30..fe182ac 100755
--- a/modules/oniguruma/config.sub
+++ b/modules/oniguruma/config.sub
@@ -1753,6 +1753,8 @@ case $kernel-$os in
 		;;
 	*-eabi* | *-gnueabi*)
 		;;
+	ios-simulator)
+		;;
 	-*)
 		# Blank kernel with real OS is always fine.
 		;;
